# SEC102 composite path proof - evidence durability (round-4 repair of R3-F3).
#
# The repository root sets `* text=auto`, and a Windows clone with
# core.autocrlf=true therefore materialises these blobs as CRLF.  Every file
# named below is byte-pinned - by a `bytes`/`sha256` pair inside a composite plan,
# by APPROVED_PROVER_BYTES/APPROVED_PROVER_SHA256 in composite_pathproof.py, or by
# a SHA-256 published in the round-1..4 self-QA - so a checkout that rewrites one
# byte makes the published FREEZE matrix unreproducible.  These rules keep the
# checked-out bytes equal to the committed bytes on every platform.
#
# Scope: this directory only.  Nothing here changes global line-ending behaviour
# and no file outside the SEC102 proof surface is affected.

# Pinned fixture blobs: treated as binary, so Git performs no end-of-line
# conversion in either direction and the committed bytes are the checked-out bytes.
sec102_r1_fixtures/** -text
sec102_r2_fixtures/** -text
sec102_r3_fixtures/** -text
sec102_r4_fixtures/** -text

# Pinned tools.  `text eol=lf` also fixes the checked-out bytes to the committed
# LF blob, but keeps both files textually diffable so the Lead can still review a
# real diff rather than "Binary files differ".  pathscope_prover.py is a FREEZE
# proof input pinned at 122446 B / 890016f0...af1d; without this line a fresh
# Windows checkout fails F4 with frozen_identity_mismatch.
pathscope_prover.py text eol=lf
composite_pathproof.py text eol=lf
